diff --git a/CLAUDE.md b/CLAUDE.md
index 241b86e..fbb6934 100644
--- a/CLAUDE.md
+++ b/CLAUDE.md
@@ -34,7 +34,7 @@ sounds and levels, then ADAM writes a **bootable .ADF** for a stock
 One object, `obj_app`, draws everything in **Draw GUI** with an immediate-mode UI
 (`scr_ui_widgets`, `scr_ui_draw`, `scr_ui_help`). Every control registers a rect
 (`ui_register`) for hover help and tutorials. Pages ("workspaces", `WS_*` in
-`scr_ws_shell`): Home, Backdrop, Levels, Sprites, Actors, Logic, Sound, Build.
+`scr_ws_shell`): Home, Backdrop, Levels, Sprites, Animate, Tiles, Actors, Logic, Sound, Music, Build.
 
 | Script | Role |
 |---|---|
@@ -58,10 +58,11 @@ with trackdisk (showing a copper loading bar) and jumps in. Registers held:
 `v_xx(a5,Dn)` with Dn = actor << ACTV_SHIFT, up to MAX_ACT = 32 actors), `a6` = $dff000.
 
 **Data block header** (offsets from data start; longs are offsets from data start, 0 = absent):
-`0 'ADAM' | 4 version | 6 flags (bit0 AGA) | 8 depth | 10 nact | 12 nrule | 14 lives | 16 show score | 18 show lives | 20 hud row | 22 hud colour | 24 msg colour | 26 player actor (-1) | 28 game block | 32 palette | 36 planes (original) | 40 actors | 44 rules | 48 sfx table | 52 game-over text | 56 win text | 60 sprite pair colours | 64 display planes | 68 copper sky (256 x $0RGB; AGA: + 256 words of low nibbles, written with LOCT) | 72 painted ground (320 words) | 76 work planes (backdrop + hills) | 80 music table | 84 second display (BOBs) | 88 BOB background` — header is 92 bytes, version 5. Music table (`M_*`, see docs/MUSIC_CONTRACT.md): nsongs word, 10 level-song bytes ($FF none), then { offset, length } of each ProTracker MOD.
+`0 'ADAM' | 4 version | 6 flags (bit0 AGA) | 8 depth | 10 nact | 12 nrule | 14 lives | 16 show score | 18 show lives | 20 hud row | 22 hud colour | 24 msg colour | 26 player actor (-1) | 28 game block | 32 palette | 36 planes (original) | 40 actors | 44 rules | 48 sfx table | 52 game-over text | 56 win text | 60 sprite pair colours | 64 display planes | 68 copper sky (256 x $0RGB; AGA: + 256 words of low nibbles, written with LOCT) | 72 painted ground (320 words) | 76 work planes (backdrop + hills) | 80 music table | 84 second display (BOBs) | 88 BOB background | 92 tile world` — header is 96 bytes, version 6. Music table (`M_*`, see docs/MUSIC_CONTRACT.md): nsongs word, 10 level-song bytes ($FF none), then { offset, length } of each ProTracker MOD.
 
 - BOBs (ADAM Pro): actors with `A_BOB` set are drawn by the blitter into a double-buffered display (`bob_draw` / `bob_flip`), wiped from the background buffer each frame; their images are the sprite's size (16-64 wide in steps of 16, 16-64 high; `A_BSIZE` = BLTSIZE), a mask then depth planes, in the nearest backdrop colours. A sprite bigger than 16 x 24 is always a BOB. Lite puts 8 actors on the disk, Pro up to 32 (actors after the 8th sprite become BOBs).
 - Animations (version 5): `A_ANIM` (actor record offset 48) points at a table of 4 x 72 bytes (`AN_*`): Idle, Walk, Jump, Fall - each { frames 1..8, rate, mode 0 loop / 1 once / 2 ping-pong, 0, 8 longs facing right, 8 longs facing left }. ADAM fills empty animations in from the others (`anim_plan` in scr_project = `anim_plan` in adf_reference.py), and writes the two-frame animation of older projects as a table too. `place_sprites` picks the animation (Jump / Fall only for roles 6-8 in the air) and the frame from `v_anim - v_astart`; the frame offset goes in `v_fofs` (bob_draw draws BOBs from it). `A_SPR2` is now only a hopper's crouch frame. With 8 directions (`anim_dirs`, `A_AMODE` bit 0) the table has 12 entries (4..11 = N NE E SE S SW W NW, picked from the move each frame via `dir_tab`, last one in `v_dir`); ADAM bakes turning round into those entries (`flip` in the plan, `DIR_CHAINS` / `anim_dir_chains`), and an empty Idle is written as mode 3 = stand facing the last direction. Fire animations (`A_AMODE` bit 1, 21 entries: 12 Fire, 13..20 Fire + N..NW) play while the player holds fire, picked from the joystick direction; the Animate page shows them on a 'With Fire' layer.
+- Tile world (version 6, `H_TILES`, `scr_tiles` / Tiles page `WS_TILES`): up to 32 tiles of 16 x 16 (`T_*` records: flags bit0 solid, bit1 dig, bit2 goal; hardness in frames, points, 4-letter name), a map up to 128 x 64 tiles (`proj.map`, byte per cell). The engine copies the map to BSS (cleared memory after the data; the bootblock allocates `loadsize + bsssize`, both poked into the last 8 bytes of boot.bin) and scrolls a 22 x 18 tile buffer every way (`cam_follow`, `draw_col` / `draw_row`, `cop_scroll`: BPLCON1 fine scroll, DDFSTRT $30, AGA FMODE 0) under a copper HUD split at line 8. Actor coordinates are world pixels (`A_XMAX` / `A_YMAX` use the map size); actors collide with solid tiles (`box_solid`, `tile_hres`, `tile_vres`, `tile_phys`). Dig and place (player only): fire + direction digs, fire alone places the carried tile, up jumps; the HUD shows the carried tile and count. Tile worlds use 8 actors, all hardware sprites (no BOBs). Example: Dig Deep (`ex_dig_deep.py`, Pro extra).
 - Actor record = 52 bytes (`A_*` equates; `A_XMAX` / `A_YMAX` = 320 - width / 256 - height are its screen limits), rule record = 16 bytes (`R_*`), sfx entry = 8 bytes (offset, length in words, Paula period), game block = `G_*` (levels, terrain colours, goal, title text, 320 heights per level).
 - **Any layout change must be made in three places: `engine.s`, `scr_adf.gml`, `tools/reference/adf_reference.py`.**
 - Roles: 0 player, 1 bouncer, 2 patrol L-R, 3 patrol U-D, 4 chaser, 5 still, 6 platform player, 7 hopper, 8 faller.
